            <div xml:id="d39">

                <pb facs="0138" n="126" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg126"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">121.866A/25: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Italy</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-02-16T18:00:00-05:00">February 16,
                            1940—6 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>39. Your 109, February 16, Noon. Mr. Taylor’s credentials are in the form of a
                    personal letter from the President. He will not make a formal address.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
